PianoWifiEthernet.cpp (the macOS side of level 6) is new code for this repository, with the same shape as this repository's
package/PianoNullEthernet/PianoNullEthernet.cpp (whose own provenance is that package's UPSTREAM): an IOEthernetController with
no device behind it — the medium published, the interface attached and marked built in, every frame dropped, the BSD wait
disabled — re-expressed here with its link left **down**, the scan list of level 6 copied onto it, and an address of this
driver's own. PianoNullEthernet is not modified, and no kext from outside this repository is linked (the native kext rule,
tooling/k27/check-native-kexts.py).

WifiApple80211.h and PianoWifi80211.h (the apple80211 front end, docs/drivers/wifi-menu.md section 5) are new code for this
repository after UniXNU-sheng's package/WifiNet.cpp (main 00ba90984e831e4c6ce30ec3d8a56e6434e9f1af, sha256
a4738ae766ded21d5a89a891c26f9a5604da37f8162ff24acc4d035776221cae; BSD-2-Clause-Patent, our own organisation's, LICENSE as above):
  Taken, re-expressed in this repository's structures and checked against the macOS 27.3 host facts (wifi-menu.md section 5.2,
  section 5.4 marks each): the request's 40-byte layout and the two ioctl numbers; the request numbers it shares with 27.3; the
  answers' layouts of POWER, STATE, OP_MODE, PHY_MODE, RSSI/NOISE, the channel and the channel list, COUNTRY_CODE, the scan
  record's head (to its elements at 0x8c) and the SCAN_REQ fields read; the card capability bits it sets; the event codes, the
  kernel event's form (vendor Apple, class 6, subclass 1, the interface's name then the payload) posted through the private
  kev_post_msg symbol, and its link-event payload; the scan's completion posted a short while after an answer from the cache;
  EIO after the last scan record. Not taken: its own ifnet and registry stand-ins (piano uses IONetworkingFamily's interface and
  an interface filter), its association, keys and data path.
  The wm4 binding bits (docs/drivers/wifi-menu.md section 9, piano-wifi-sheng; read at the 2026-11-15 clone e578007, the study
  private/host-checks/20261115-unixnu-sheng): the SIOCGIFMEDIA answer words (IFM_IEEE80211|IFM_AUTO, IFM_AVALID, count 1), their
  if_ioctl form re-expressed in this repository's interface filter; card capability bit 46 and what it makes the framework's scan
  wait for; the scan request's type field at 0x34 (3: the held results); SSID_CHANGED and BSSID_CHANGED beside every
  LINK_CHANGED; and, from package/ShengEthernet.cpp (same licence, same clone), NativeSandboxGrantProcess on the interface — here
  the single name "airportd", because this kernel's native_sandbox_grant compares the whole property. Their macOS-27.3 finding
  that a user-client request's byte replies must be memcpy'd, not copyout'd, is the shape of the kext's fallback (shengKernelBuffer),
  with this repository's own bounds logic; their comma-separated grant list cannot match this kernel and is not used.
OpenIntelWireless (itlwm / AirportItlwm, GPL) was not read for this code; its facts reached the design only through the W0
report's notes (private/host-checks/20261114-io80211), and none of its text is here.

